  <wpt lat="49.718543021008372" lon="-113.45114903524518">
    <ele>0</ele>
    <time>2026-08-24T14:43:26Z</time>
    <name>Oldman River Provincial Recreation Area (no water, pit toilets)</name>
    <cmt>description: no water / pit toilets &lt;br&gt;"Sewage	&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The sewage disposal station here is permanently closed. The nearby Town of Fort Macleod operates a public sewage disposal and potable water station (located on the east side of the town next to Mac's Convenience Store).&lt;br&gt;Water&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You are expected to bring your own water. Government of Alberta regulations require that water from pumps/taps like the one located here NOT be used for drinking, cooking or washing (including brushing teeth and washing dishes). Water from the pump/tap onsite can only be used for purposes like putting out a campfire.&lt;br&gt;"&lt;br&gt;https://albertaparks.ca/parks/south/oldman-river-pra/information-facilities/camping/oldman-river/&lt;br&gt;Type: Provincial Park Campground&lt;br&gt;ID:</cmt>
    <desc>description: no water / pit toilets &lt;br&gt;"Sewage	&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The sewage disposal station here is permanently closed. The nearby Town of Fort Macleod operates a public sewage disposal and potable water station (located on the east side of the town next to Mac's Convenience Store).&lt;br&gt;Water&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You are expected to bring your own water. Government of Alberta regulations require that water from pumps/taps like the one located here NOT be used for drinking, cooking or washing (including brushing teeth and washing dishes). Water from the pump/tap onsite can only be used for purposes like putting out a campfire.&lt;br&gt;"&lt;br&gt;https://albertaparks.ca/parks/south/oldman-river-pra/information-facilities/camping/oldman-river/&lt;br&gt;Type: Provincial Park Campground&lt;br&gt;ID:</desc>
    <sym>Campground</sym>
    <type>user</type>
    <extensions>
      <gpxx:WaypointExtension>
        <gpxx:DisplayMode>SymbolAndName</gpxx:DisplayMode>
